---

{{ echo |> markdown }}
Inspired by [Vale’s Halo stats](https://vale.rocks/posts/halo-stats), then [further encouraged](https://fedi.vale.rocks/objects/6d86daed-5066-4f1d-b9bb-99f591925f12), I managed to dig out my **Uncharted 2: Among Thieves** multiplayer stats… I don’t know that these captured the very last game I ever played but it’s gotta be dang close. Part historical account and part data visualisation, I’m going to take a trip down memory lane, if you want to follow along.
{{ /echo }}

{{ callout 'Wet paint, do not touch!' }}Welcome to my first art-directed post! This page will respect your system preferences, with the theme picker disabled. Also don’t ask if I bought the exact font from Uncharted 2 just for this page, that’d be _ridiculous_. (and if you’re seeing this in your RSS reader, know this post will look a little better on my web site){{ /callout }}

{{ echo |> markdown }}
## Where it began

I used to run a fansite called **JAKPRO**, all about Jak & Daxter — a PlayStation 2 series developed by Naughty Dog, of Crash Bandicoot fame. However, after some time, it became obvious the Jak franchise was abandoned (The Lost Frontier wasn’t the revival we had hoped for…), and being an all-around Naughty Dog fan, I pivoted to making a fansite about all their major games, named **The Naughty Kennel** (which, in retrospect, was a _terrible_ name for search engine optimisation purposes, but The Kennel was already taken).

During that time (starting on JAKPRO, and eventually migrated over to the Naughty Kennel), I had created a "stats card" service, since Naughty Dog made player stats available on the web, at a URL like this one (archived and outdated): [http://www.naughtydog.com/stats/index/JaKhris](https://web.archive.org/web/20100106001534/http://www.naughtydog.com/stats/index/JaKhris). I did this because it was the perfect storm — it would require some design skills: check; some coding skills: check; public access to user data: check; and a passion for the whole thing: check.
{{ /echo }}

{{ set imageUrl = './generator-u2-jp.avif' |> toRoot }}
{{ image imageUrl, "The generator for Uncharted 2 on JAKPRO.net, a stylised form asking you to provide your username and select a character and background to decorate the image. A total user count of 14599 is displayed as well as some milestones below.", "Rough but functional", { ratio: "1200/753" } }}

{{ echo |> markdown }}
I created a PHP script to scrape the page of a given user (there were actually 4 pages to scrape per user), discovering the joys of HTML parsing via regular expression, and rate-limiting from both my web host, and from the stats site. I was eventually provided a — get this — _documented_ API by Naughty Dog themselves, who were very supportive. And on the other side of things, I’d see the user count grow, and randomly stumble upon a card on a message board (back when social media hadn’t killed that side of the web yet). I wasn’t solving a global crisis, but it felt cool being part of… _something_, you know?
{{ /echo }}

{{ callout 'Fun fact (but also: brag)' }}I got to play the **Uncharted 2 closed beta** with the (now ex-) co-president of Naughty Dog, **Christophe Balestra**, who’d sent me a download code (maybe more of a company-wide effort to promote the game than anything, but still). We played a game of a co-op together, microphones working across oceans, and completed a mission successfully! Also it turned out his brother lived in my city at the time (he’s French, too). Small world.{{ /callout }}

{{ echo |> markdown }}
## More data

A few years after, when I built The Naughty Kennel, instead of just storing some basic ID and last updated info, since I was scraping all this data anyways, I figured I could create leaderboards, which were not available on Naughty Dog’s pages, to make it a little more community-oriented. So, I naturally created the world’s least optimised database table, with over 140 columns, capturing the main data provided on Uncharted 2’s player stats page, including kills and deaths for each of the 16 weapons, and also the count for each of the 63 medals you could earn, plus a handful for metadata.
{{ /echo }}

{{ set imageUrl = './generator-u2-nk.avif' |> toRoot }}
{{ image imageUrl, "The generator for Uncharted 2 on Naughty-Kennel.com, a stylised form asking you to provide your username and select a character and background to decorate the image. A total user count of 12231 is displayed as well as some milestones below.", "Kinda sorta better?", { ratio: "1200/753" } }}

{{ echo |> markdown }}
I had totally forgotten about this feature until I revived my project files, but there it was, with a grand total of **13,573 entries** of player data (if you played and had a card, there’s a very slight chance I might have yours, too!). The last data capture would occur on January 13th of 2013, shortly before The Naughty Kennel’s servers would shut down for good. Fansites were becoming less popular due to social media, I was more focused on my studies, and I didn’t have the time (or motivation, frankly) to keep the site alive, despite all the goodwill of the remaining community and folks helping me run the site…

The game’s online servers, along with Naughty Dog’s stats pages, have long since closed as well (on the 3rd of September 2019, alongside those of Uncharted 3 and The Last of Us) but [you can’t stop modders](https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3493685058). I found my own data in this backup, which wasn’t that hard to find, since I was the first entry in that table… but looking at it on the revived Naughty Kennel web site let me take a look at the leaderboards, so here’s a little insight into the top players, as recorded in my database:
- **Im-Me-21** with 22,387 games played (and a respectable K/D ratio of 2.48)
- **hg-700** with $1,660,972,488 earned (the game’s equivalent of experience points)
- **The-Legend-10** with 347,794 kills
- **JaKhris** (that’s me) was ranked 2,461st of those 13,573 players

It’s funny looking at the leaderboards again now and remembering some usernames of players that absolutely demolished me, such as [triplewreck](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4f4iwAAFn8k) who never missed (K/D ratio of 4.23!), or **gloomcool** who was a prolific cheater, glitching through walls, making public online matches extremely unenjoyable. Every game would be “recorded”, which you could replay in the Machinima mode to create your own clips (like the montage linked above), which was very exciting at the time. Uncharted 3 even let you upload straight to YouTube (no capture card needed!) and Naughty Dog would feature some curated clips alongside official videos on the Uncharted TV player, on the multiplayer menu.

## So… you said something about cards?

Sorry for yapping so much, this is very nostalgic for me! Here’s what my **actual** stats card looked like on its very last run. It’s dense and definitely not WCAG-compliant, but it did cram lots of information into 62,500 pixels, built using PHP’s GD image library to composite the data on one of the 70 background templates I made:
{{ /echo }}

{{ set imageUrl = [assets.images, 'u2-card-jakhris.png'] |> toPath }}
{{ image imageUrl, "My stats card for Uncharted 2 online, showing I reached level 60, with a kill-death ratio of 1.14, and 17,755 games played, and a last game played on June 4th, 2011.", "Ooh, the crunchy, low-res nostalgia…", { ratio: "500/125" } }}

{{ echo |> markdown }}
With that out of the way, let’s see if I can present the data, as it was a decade ago, but neatly…
{{ /echo }}

<div class="uncharted2-stats-main" id="uncharted2-stats">
    <img src="./psn-avatar.png" alt="" width="160" height="160" class="uncharted2-stats-pic" loading="lazy">
    
    <dl class="uncharted2-stats-list">
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-username">
            <dt class="visually-hidden">Username</dt>
            <dd class="grouper grouper--center-block">
                <img src="./level-{{ uncharted2.level }}.png" alt="" width="50" height="50" class="uncharted2-stats-username-rank" loading="lazy">
                <span class="uncharted2-stats-username-text h1">{{ uncharted2.psn_username }}</span>
            </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-level">
            <dt>Level</dt>
            <dd class="fontVariant-tabularNums">{{ uncharted2.level }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-cash">
            <dt>Cash</dt>
            <dd class="fontVariant-tabularNums">$&zwnj;{{ uncharted2.cash |> formatNumber }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-time">
            <dt>Total Play Time</dt>
            <dd class="fontVariant-tabularNums">{{ uncharted2.time_played |> timeTag({ isDuration: true, regular: true }) }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-date">
            <dt>Last Game</dt>
            <dd id="u2-last-game-date">{{ uncharted2.last_game |> timeTag({ regular: true }) }}</dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
</div>

<div class="uncharted2-stats-section">
    <div class="uncharted2-stats-2up">
        <div class="uncharted2-stats-2up-item flow">
            <h2 class="uncharted2-stats-2up-title textAlign-center">
                <span data-u2-mode="competitive" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span>Competitive</span>
            </h2>

            <p class="uncharted2-stats-ring" style="--flow-space: var(--size-l); --stats-ring-ratio: {{ uncharted2.competitive.kills / (uncharted2.competitive.kills + uncharted2.competitive.deaths) }};">
                {{# To use the value from the kd_ratio prop… (1/(D / (K+D)))-1 = K/D #}}
                <span class="uncharted2-stats-ring-label">
                    <abbr title="Kill/Death Ratio" aria-hidden="true">K/D</abbr>
                    <span class="visually-hidden">Kill-Death Ratio</span>
                </span>
                <span class="uncharted2-stats-ring-value">{{ uncharted2.competitive.kd_ratio }}</span>
            </p>

            <dl class="uncharted2-stats-def">
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Kills</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.kills |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Deaths</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.deaths |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Assists</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.assists |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Treasures</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.treasures_captured |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Territories</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.territories_captured |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Games</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.games_played |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Wins</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.wins |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="uncharted2-stats-def-inline">
                    <dt>Losses</dt>
                    <dd>{{ uncharted2.competitive.losses |> formatNumber }}</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </div>

